  "review": {
    "change": "Returned VM spawn error now produces cleanup unknown. Actual run\u2192dispatch\u2192receive source retains original transport/rawReport/recognizedReport/error. Unknown cleanup closes only its two actual raw handles, including all lost/error prefixes. Pre-spawn image failure still has the distinct not_started branch.",
    "finding": "The broad actual spawn relation permits a committed child on a returned error. VM.run previously reported not_started, which cleanupRun treated as authorization to remove its backing directory.",
    "fixture": "Actual fresh RunDirectory.create, exclusive policy write, shared VM/receive/cleanupRun source and retained-parent name/data lookup. The spawn reply is synthetic; no child/QEMU/VM workload is run on the host. The fixture uses the real decoder to produce a recognized report prefix, and confirms exact known/raw report preservation plus retained files/name. Test cleanup is performed separately after certifying that the fixture started no child.",
    "proof_boundary": "No no-child-on-error assumption was added. These source proofs do not establish process reaping; truthful runtime wait and owned process tokens remain individual runtime/lifetime interfaces.",
    "scope_extension": "This records the new VM error behavior separately from the frozen earlier VM source/profile review. No unrelated theorem/claim or historical evidence was rebound."
  },
